waiver: harness-limit
reason: the program stops through exit(134). The wasmtime command line
  reports each exit status above 125 as 1, so the wasm legs cannot observe
  134. On arm64-darwin a worker body runs in the process of the program,
  and the runtime does not know that a worker runs, so `exit` there still
  ends the program with its own status (#15051). The interpreters and the
  Linux and Android legs pin the status.
